      "case": "leaves/locale/context-absent-explicit-and-default",
      "discriminates": "absent and explicitly-default are different states that read identically through FromContext: only HasLocale separates them, and session.go:1359 installs the session locale precisely when it is false. A Rust port modelling the carrier as Option<Locale> must keep Some(Default) distinct from None. The trace also pins that a nested WithLocale overrides rather than merges, and that a failed parse still stores whatever Locale the caller was handed -- for `not a locale` that is the zero tag, so a rejected --locale reads back as present-and-default, byte for byte the state an explicit WithLocale(Default) produces and still distinct from absent",
