      "case": "leaves/locale/translation-fallback-matching",
      "discriminates": "the fallback is language.NewMatcher's, not a prefix match: base-only tags, sibling regions and script variants either reach a table at confidence >= Low or fall through to English. The matcher entry is zh-TW (loc_generated.go:18), a different canonical tag from the zh-Hant-TW this group also parses, so zh-HK/zh-MO/zh-Hant reaching a table and pt-PT reaching pt-BR are the rows a hand-written fallback chain gets wrong, and yue/wuu/nl-NL/ar-SA fix where the threshold actually cuts off. Type_expected_1110 is requested beside Modules_6244 for the reason given in leaves/locale/translation-shipped-locales: fr-FR's Modules_6244 is byte-identical to English, so fr-CA selecting the French table is only witnessed on the second key. en-GB is a negative control rather than a witness in either key: English is matcher index 0 with a nil table entry (loc_generated.go:33), so its answer is the untranslated text by construction",
      "go_authority": "tsc/internal/diagnostics/loc_generated.go:15-30 language.NewMatcher over [en, zh-CN, zh-TW, cs-CZ, de-DE, es-ES, fr-FR, it-IT, ja-JP, ko-KR, pl-PL, pt-BR, ru-RU, tr-TR]; diagnostics.go:104-109 accepts the match when confidence >= language.Low and the index is inside localeFuncs",
